35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The actual time for a full pass is about 102 minutes total. Also, an outside firm requires us to tidy up before they arrive, meaning we'd still have some work to do.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I found out that some of us are away for a week or more almost every month, and most of the kitchen mess comes from just two or three people.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The house chat shows that our only arguments started with reminders about undone chores, and the previous tenants warned that permanent room assignments led to them barely speaking.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"We're wasting money! We have three bottles of the same spray, and we're spending 2,300 yen a month on supplies. Also, the management office charges 4,200 yen an hour for a cleaner.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"It turns out we all have different ideas of what ""done"" means, and the bathroom grout gets black spots back in just eleven days because of the poor ventilation.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, if the grout returns in eleven days regardless of effort, a strict rota might just lead to frustration rather than actual cleanliness.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, that's true, but if only a few of us are actually using the kitchen, it's even more frustrating for the others to have to clean it on a rota!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, your point about usage is valid, but we must be careful. If we assign work based on usage, we risk creating a hierarchy that could lead to the same resentment the previous tenants faced.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"But if we just pay for a cleaner, we can stop fighting about who did what! Though 4,200 yen an hour is a lot, maybe it's worth it to keep the peace?","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I'm worried that even with a cleaner, we'll still disagree on whether the house is actually clean enough, since we all have different standards for what ""done"" means.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, that is a fair point. If we can't agree on a standard, any system we choose will eventually fail. We need a method that removes the ambiguity of ""done.""","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"Maybe a professional cleaner would solve that? They have their own standards, so we wouldn't have to argue about whether the basin is just wiped or actually scrubbed!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"That is a logical point, Mio. A professional standard would provide an objective benchmark, potentially removing the personal friction that leads to the arguments I found in the chat.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"And it would solve the money problem too! If we have one bill from a company, we can just split it evenly instead of guessing who bought the sponges!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I suppose a professional would be more consistent, but I'm still worried about the cost and whether we'd still have to tidy up first.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, the tidying is a small price to pay compared to the 102 minutes of deep cleaning we'd save. It seems a professional service addresses the most objective issues we've found.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,I agree! It's way better than a rota where people who don't even cook have to scrub the stove while others are away on vacation. It feels like the most fair option.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. Given the previous tenants' warning about permanent assignments and our history of friction over reminders, a neutral third party is the safest way to preserve our relationships.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'm all for it! It's the best way to make sure the money is handled properly and we don't have to be detectives about the sponges anymore!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"If everyone else is on board and it means I don't have to worry about the bathroom grout or different standards, then I'm okay with it too.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
